---
layout: changelog
title: Announcing Appwrite 2.1 for self-hosted deployments
date: 2026-09-14
cover: /images/blog/appwrite-2-1-self-hosted/cover.avif
tags: storage, auth, console, infrastructure
---

Appwrite 2.1 is now available for self-hosting.

This release includes:

- The [S3 API](/blog/post/announcing-s3-api) for Storage at `/v1/s3`, so the AWS CLI, AWS SDKs, rclone, and other S3 clients can read and write files in your buckets
- [AutoGravity](/blog/post/introducing-autogravity) as a new `appwrite-autogravity` container. Set `_APP_AUTOGRAVITY_HOST` to turn on AutoGravity
- TikTok and Kakao as OAuth2 providers
- A batch of fixes to Appwrite Console
- Runtimes for Dart 3.13 and Flutter 3.47

Head over to our [migration guide](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/production/updates) to upgrade your instance. Upgrade to 2.0.0 first if you are still on 1.9.x.

For the complete list of updates and fixes, check out the [release notes](https://github.com/appwrite/appwrite/releases/tag/2.1.0) on GitHub.

